    {
      "id": "med-an-01",
      "type": "mcq",
      "theme": "analyse",
      "category": "Limites",
      "prompt": "La limite $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x \\to 0^+} x \\ln x$ vaut :",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$0$",
          "isCorrect": true
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$-\\infty$",
          "isCorrect": false
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$1$",
          "isCorrect": false
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "N'existe pas",
          "isCorrect": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Forme $0 \\times (-\\infty)$. On pose $t = -\\ln x \\to +\\infty$ : $x\\ln x = -te^{-t} \\to 0$ par croissance comparée. Résultat fondamental du programme."
    },
    {
      "id": "med-an-02",
      "type": "mcq",
      "theme": "analyse",
      "category": "Dérivation",
      "prompt": "Le nombre de solutions de $e^x = 3x$ sur $\\mathbb{R}$ est :",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$2$",
          "isCorrect": true
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$0$",
          "isCorrect": false
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$1$",
          "isCorrect": false
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$3$",
          "isCorrect": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "Soit $g(x) = e^x - 3x$. $g'(x) = e^x - 3 = 0 \\Leftrightarrow x = \\ln 3$. $g(\\ln 3) = 3-3\\ln 3 < 0$ car $\\ln 3 > 1$. Or $\\displaystyle \\lim_{-\\infty}g = +\\infty$, $g(0)=1>0$ et $\\displaystyle \\lim_{+\\infty}g=+\\infty$. Le TVI donne $2$ changements de signe : une racine sur $]-\\infty, \\ln 3[$ et une sur $]\\ln 3, +\\infty[$."
    },
    {
      "id": "med-an-03",
      "type": "mcq",
      "theme": "analyse",
      "category": "Dérivation",
      "prompt": "Soit $f(x) = x^3 - 3x + 1$. Le nombre de racines réelles de $f$ est :",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "$3$",
          "isCorrect": true
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "$1$",
          "isCorrect": false
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "$2$",
          "isCorrect": false
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "$0$",
          "isCorrect": false
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "$f'(x)=3(x-1)(x+1)$. $f(-1)=3>0$ (max local), $f(1)=-1<0$ (min local). Avec $\\displaystyle \\lim_{\\pm\\infty}=\\pm\\infty$, le TVI donne $3$ changements de signe, donc $3$ racines distinctes."
    },
